cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EDN-S: Satellite Image Super-Resolution"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chekalil"
    given-names: "Aimene Charef Eddine"
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aimenachraff-jpg/EDN-s"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/edns/"
keywords:
  - super-resolution
  - satellite imagery
  - Sentinel-2
  - ALSAT-2B
  - EDSR
  - deep learning
  - PyTorch
  - remote sensing
  - hallucination detection
abstract: >-
  EDN-S is a PyTorch implementation of an EDSR-small super-resolution model for
  four-band satellite imagery. It includes training and reconstruction code, a
  tiled GeoTIFF inference path, a spectral and spatial quality metric suite, and
  reference-based hallucination detection. The reported experiments use Sentinel-2
  imagery with a simulated ALSAT-2B x4 degradation; no real ALSAT-2B data was used.
